      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(code-mode): use Object.hasOwn instead of Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty.call",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\n`Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty.call(obj, key)` and `Object.hasOwn(obj, key)` are semantically identical — both check own properties only, skipping inherited prototype keys. The modern `Object.hasOwn` is shorter, more readable, and not susceptible to a custom `hasOwnProperty` property on the target object.\n\n## Changes\n\n- **`src/agents/code-mode.worker.ts`**: Replace `Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty.call(baseTools, name)` with `Object.hasOwn(baseTools, name)` in the baseTools deduplication check.\n- **`src/agents/code-mode.test.ts`**: Add test verifying that prototype-named tool identifiers (toString, __proto__, constructor, hasOwnProperty) are safely handled without throwing.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Existing tests pass: `pnpm test src/agents/code-mode.test.ts`\n- New test `\"rejects prototype-named tool identifiers in baseTools registration\"` passes: confirms prototype-named tools do not trigger errors\n- Pure mechanical refactor — no behavior change",
        "branch": "fix/code-mode-use-object-hasown",
